      "amount": "1 cup"
    },
    {
      "name": "coconut milk",
      "amount": "1/2 cup"
    }
  ],
  "instructions": [
    "Heat the olive oil in the clay tagine vessel over medium heat.",
    "Add the sliced onion and cook until softened, about 5 minutes.",
    "Add the minced garlic and grated ginger and cook for 1 minute.",
    "Add the cumin, coriander, and cayenne pepper and cook for 1 minute.",
    "Add the katsuramuki-cut chicken and cook until browned, about 5 minutes.",
    "Add the chicken broth and coconut milk and bring to a simmer.",
    "Reduce the heat to low and cook, covered, for 20 minutes.",
    "Stir in the white flour to thicken the sauce.",
    "Cook for an additional 5 minutes, or until the sauce has thickened.",
    "Serve hot, garnished with fresh herbs.",
    "Ensure poultry is cooked to an internal temperature of 74°C / 165°F (juices run clear, no pink remaining) before serving."
  ],
